  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35734100",
      "title": "Controlling Which Data Should Be Deferred",
      "sourceHash": "65745b0af1db23c6a8d2d170cec4568c14757c80e4ad4c1f994101a1897831f2",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 4.17,
          "en": "So, how does this defer feature shine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.17,
          "end": 7.62,
          "en": "if you have multiple requests with different speeds?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.62,
          "end": 10.5,
          "en": "Well, for that, let's go to the event detail page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.5,
          "end": 13.29,
          "en": "Here we're only outputting the event item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.29,
          "end": 15.27,
          "en": "but I'm going to change this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.27,
          "end": 16.83,
          "en": "Besides the event item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.83,
          "end": 20.463,
          "en": "I also wanna output my events list here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.66,
          "end": 24.6,
          "en": "So therefore, we of course must fetch the events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.6,
          "end": 26.463,
          "en": "on this page here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.72,
          "end": 29.97,
          "en": "To do that, I'll quickly copy that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.97,
          "end": 32.91,
          "en": "load events function from events.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.91,
          "end": 35.67,
          "en": "We could also store it in another shared file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.67,
          "end": 38.97,
          "en": "and export it, but here I'll quickly copy it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.97,
          "end": 41.28,
          "en": "and paste it here above my loader",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.28,
          "end": 43.203,
          "en": "in the EventDetail.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.12,
          "end": 46.98,
          "en": "I will also add another function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.98,
          "end": 50.763,
          "en": "in this EventDetail.js file, which I'll name loadEvent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.6,
          "end": 55.29,
          "en": "where I expect to get the ID of an event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.29,
          "end": 57.27,
          "en": "and I'll put that code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.27,
          "end": 60.24,
          "en": "which is responsible for loading a single event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.24,
          "end": 62.973,
          "en": "into this loadEvent helper function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.83,
          "end": 67.47,
          "en": "Now, just as before, I will also change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.47,
          "end": 70.77,
          "en": "this return value here of load event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.77,
          "end": 74.1,
          "en": "to manually extract the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.1,
          "end": 77.43,
          "en": "So just as in load events, I'll use the JSON method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.43,
          "end": 81.693,
          "en": "and await it, and then return resData.event here in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.55,
          "end": 85.47,
          "en": "So now I got these two helper functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.47,
          "end": 88.39,
          "en": "and I will now use it here in this loader function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.67,
          "end": 93.663,
          "en": "because here I now want to actually defer again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.59,
          "end": 96.45,
          "en": "so I will return defer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.45,
          "end": 99.423,
          "en": "and for that of course we must import defer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.8,
          "end": 104.00999999999999,
          "en": "and I will defer here because we know that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.00999999999999,
          "end": 106.83,
          "en": "load events will take a while because we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.83,
          "end": 109.62,
          "en": "this two second time out on the backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.62,
          "end": 113.00999999999999,
          "en": "whereas load event should be rather fast.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.00999999999999,
          "end": 116.16,
          "en": "And I wanna show you how defer can help you load some data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.16,
          "end": 118.443,
          "en": "whilst still waiting for other data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.34,
          "end": 122.85,
          "en": "So here, when calling defer, I pass an object to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.85,
          "end": 126.21,
          "en": "and I have my single event where I will call",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.21,
          "end": 128.85,
          "en": "loadEvent and pass this ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.85,
          "end": 131.613,
          "en": "which I'm extracting from my params, to load event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.02,
          "end": 137.82,
          "en": "and I have events where I call loadEvents, like that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.82,
          "end": 139.97,
          "en": "and of course that should also be executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.82,
          "end": 144.3,
          "en": "So now this is looking similar to what we had before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 144.3,
          "end": 147.93,
          "en": "in the events.js file, but we have two requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 147.93,
          "end": 150.123,
          "en": "that are bundled in this defer object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.99,
          "end": 154.82999999999998,
          "en": "Now with that done, we're using useRouteLoaderData here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 154.82999999999998,
          "end": 159.72,
          "en": "but that works with defer just as used loader data did.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 159.72,
          "end": 160.86,
          "en": "And we know that here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 160.86,
          "end": 165.81,
          "en": "we'll get an object that has an event and an events key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 165.81,
          "end": 169.083,
          "en": "These are these two deferred requests so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 170.49,
          "end": 174.9,
          "en": "Now we need the await component, which I showed you before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 174.9,
          "end": 179.28,
          "en": "and we use that await component two times",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 179.28,
          "end": 181.863,
          "en": "to await these two different requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 182.79,
          "end": 187.26,
          "en": "So here I pass event to the resolve prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 187.26,
          "end": 191.313,
          "en": "and then I pass events plural to the resolve prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 193.59,
          "end": 196.29,
          "en": "Then we got these dynamic values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 196.29,
          "end": 199.17000000000002,
          "en": "between the opening and closing await tags",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 199.17000000000002,
          "end": 202.74,
          "en": "where I got my event in this first case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 202.74,
          "end": 205.56,
          "en": "or let's maybe name it loadedEvent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 205.56,
          "end": 207.57,
          "en": "where I then wanna output the event item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 207.57,
          "end": 209.1,
          "en": "once that data is there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 209.1,
          "end": 214.1,
          "en": "So here I pass loadedEvent to the event prop, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 218.46,
          "end": 220.773,
          "en": "And then here, for the second await block,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 221.88,
          "end": 226.88,
          "en": "I got my loaded events, and I will output those here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 230.19,
          "end": 232.11,
          "en": "Now we also need suspense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 232.11,
          "end": 235.2,
          "en": "and every await block must be wrapped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 235.2,
          "end": 237.3,
          "en": "with its own suspense component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 237.3,
          "end": 240.78,
          "en": "Otherwise, suspense will wait for both awaits to complete",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 240.78,
          "end": 243.99,
          "en": "before showing anything, which is not what we want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 243.99,
          "end": 246.03,
          "en": "So we need to import suspense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 246.03,
          "end": 248.283,
          "en": "and then add our fallback here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 250.08,
          "end": 253.5,
          "en": "Again, a paragraph where we maybe say loading,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 253.5,
          "end": 258.5,
          "en": "with that inline style added here, like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 260.94,
          "end": 263.46,
          "en": "and I'll use that same suspense block down there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 263.46,
          "end": 265.173,
          "en": "to wrap my second await.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 267.15,
          "end": 268.95,
          "en": "Now what does this do?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 268.95,
          "end": 270.87,
          "en": "Well, if we saved at all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 270.87,
          "end": 274.479,
          "en": "and I click on an event, you'll see that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 274.479,
          "end": 277.53,
          "en": "the details were there basically immediately,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 277.53,
          "end": 280.40999999999997,
          "en": "but the list of events was still loading.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 280.40999999999997,
          "end": 282.21,
          "en": "Let's take a look at this again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 282.21,
          "end": 285.27,
          "en": "If I go to my events, and I click on a single event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 285.27,
          "end": 287.64,
          "en": "the details are there immediately,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 287.64,
          "end": 290.64300000000003,
          "en": "and the other list of events is still loading.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 291.87,
          "end": 292.703,
          "en": "By the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 292.703,
          "end": 296.43,
          "en": "those links in this nested list would now be broken.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 296.43,
          "end": 299.85,
          "en": "To fix that, we would have to go to EventsList.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 299.85,
          "end": 303.99,
          "en": "and then convert these links to absolute links here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 303.99,
          "end": 306.63,
          "en": "since we can now end up in situations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 306.63,
          "end": 310.11,
          "en": "where this component is rendered on a page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 310.11,
          "end": 312.42,
          "en": "where adding this to the currently active path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 312.42,
          "end": 315.093,
          "en": "would lead to an overall incorrect path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 317.04,
          "end": 318.69,
          "en": "But that's just a tiny side note",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 318.69,
          "end": 321.96,
          "en": "not related to deferring data loading.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 321.96,
          "end": 323.52,
          "en": "But what we do get with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 323.52,
          "end": 327.33,
          "en": "is now a page that's instantly available, while still",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 327.33,
          "end": 330.57,
          "en": "loading other data that's not instantly available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 330.57,
          "end": 333.273,
          "en": "However, this is still not the perfect solution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 334.26,
          "end": 336.54,
          "en": "The backend here is super fast,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 336.54,
          "end": 340.26,
          "en": "but you can sometimes see a loading message here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 340.26,
          "end": 344.43,
          "en": "for these details, for a short fraction of a second",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 344.43,
          "end": 348.36,
          "en": "because we're actually deferring both pieces of data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 348.36,
          "end": 350.403,
          "en": "the single event and all events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 351.65999999999997,
          "end": 354.93,
          "en": "Now, it would make sense to tell React Router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 354.93,
          "end": 356.94,
          "en": "that it should maybe wait",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 356.94,
          "end": 359.76,
          "en": "with displaying the event detail page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 359.76,
          "end": 361.56,
          "en": "until the details have been loaded,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 361.56,
          "end": 363.57,
          "en": "so the navigation should only start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 363.57,
          "end": 365.82,
          "en": "once the details have been loaded,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 365.82,
          "end": 368.22,
          "en": "but it should then load the list of events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 368.22,
          "end": 370.59,
          "en": "after we navigate it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 370.59,
          "end": 374.043,
          "en": "and defer gives you that fine grain control.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 375.21,
          "end": 379.02,
          "en": "If you have an async loader with the async function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 379.02,
          "end": 381.72,
          "en": "you can simply add the await keyword here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 381.72,
          "end": 384.45,
          "en": "and that will make sure that defer waits",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 384.45,
          "end": 386.19,
          "en": "for this data to be loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 386.19,
          "end": 388.86,
          "en": "before loading this page component at all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 388.86,
          "end": 393.093,
          "en": "so before moving and navigating to this page component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 393.99,
          "end": 397.47,
          "en": "but will load this data, the loadEvents data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 397.47,
          "end": 399.423,
          "en": "after the page was loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 400.26,
          "end": 403.77,
          "en": "So await is your lever, your switch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 403.77,
          "end": 407.1,
          "en": "for controlling which data should be awaited",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 407.1,
          "end": 408.93,
          "en": "before moving to this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 408.93,
          "end": 411.65999999999997,
          "en": "and which data should be deferred,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 411.65999999999997,
          "end": 416.15999999999997,
          "en": "so where you wanna load the data after moving to the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 416.15999999999997,
          "end": 417.96,
          "en": "And with this setup here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 417.96,
          "end": 420.57,
          "en": "we would wait for the event details to be loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 420.57,
          "end": 423.33,
          "en": "before loading this page component at all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 423.33,
          "end": 425.49,
          "en": "but we would load the list of events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 425.49,
          "end": 427.473,
          "en": "after rendering this page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 428.52,
          "end": 430.89,
          "en": "Here, you won't see a big difference,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 430.89,
          "end": 433.2,
          "en": "but it will actually ensure that we never see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 433.2,
